The statute's retention rule states that records of the society are retained for the period named in the schedule of this statute [[cite:obs-1c39313618ea9b634cebcfd8b7b1c085e9fea1af "Records of the society are retained for the period named in the schedule of this statute."]]. According to the schedule, ledgers are kept for eleven calendar years and are shredded afterwards [[cite:obs-ed4e25601de0bcc342236e954c75b57431241541 "Ledgers: eleven calendar years, shredding afterwards."]].